# rl_capture.kfl - the capture surface's spellings, for the round trip.
#
# Three things a programme can write about a docking interface are
# written here so that printing the parsed tree back out and parsing it
# again reproduces them: the block a programme declares its own capture
# envelope in, the clause that names which port an observe is measured
# against, and the mark that asks that observe for its two optional
# channels.
#
# The declared envelope is not named by any port here. That is
# deliberate and it is what makes the fixture useful for what it is
# for: the ports come from assets this tree already ships, which name
# the envelope the compiler defines, and the block is present so its
# spelling is pinned beside the two clauses without a new asset having
# to ship with it.
#
# The task is a stand-in and not a benchmark. A servicer approaches a
# derelict, the reward pays for closing the gap, and the episode ends
# on contact.

form RL_CAPTURE

fn world w
    astro_body earth gm=3.986004418e14 mass=5.972e24

    capture_envelope grasp_s
        axial_rate 0 0.050000000000000003
        lateral_rate 0.02
        pitchyaw_rate 3
        roll_rate 3
        lateral 0.050000000000000003
        pitchyaw 10
        roll 180
        diameter 700
    end

    astro_body servicer assembly="../examples/assets/servicer_2t.k26asm" parent=earth pos_x=7.0e6 pos_y=0.0 pos_z=0.0 vel_x=0.0 vel_y=7546.0 vel_z=0.0 quat_w=1.0 quat_x=0.0 quat_y=0.0 quat_z=0.0

    astro_body derelict assembly="../examples/assets/derelict_satellite.k26asm" parent=earth pos_x=7.0e6 pos_y=30.0 pos_z=0.0 vel_x=0.0 vel_y=7546.0 vel_z=0.0 quat_w=0.0 quat_x=0.0 quat_y=1.0 quat_z=0.0

    episode
        control_dt 0.5
        horizon 64
        substeps 5
        terminated when hit_hit > 0.5
    end

    action push box -1.0 1.0 default 0.0

    observe port forward of servicer against dock of derelict full as dock
    observe contact of servicer as hit

    objective
        reward 0.0 - dock_axial
    end
end

end
